{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291023-lunars-inspiration","id":1291023,"title":"Lunars Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-23T00:24:32-08:00","id":1291023,"title":"Lunars Inspiration","content":"Given the amount of juicy concepts and plot hooks the backer previews have provided us with, I figured maybe a thread dedicated to works that can also be mined for Lunar inspiration might be useful.<br /> <br /> First, links to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290856-tier-zoo-lunars\">BrilliantRain's Tier Zoo</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289959-dragon-marked-for-death-being-terrestrial-lunar-and-infernal-at-the-same-time\">Sunder The Gold's Dragon Marked For Death</a> threads that started the thought.<br /> <br /> And second, the trailer to The Liar Princess And The Blind Prince game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UdBespMvxaA&amp;app=desktop\" data-code=\"UdBespMvxaA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UdBespMvxaA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> There's some good stuff in here!<br /> <br /> - The Witch absolutely is a No Moon shahan-ya.<br /> - This also brings home the more wide-reaching effects the Immaculate Doctrine can have. In an Exalted sense, the 'true self' the princess is hiding is not the massive beast she can transform into, but her identity as a Lunar that represents.<br /> - So an understandable reason to panic and claw a guy's eyes out on him seeing it!<br /> - This could also be a Solar-Lunar bond.<br /> - The Realm version of this fairytale probably goes very differently.<br /> <br /> What about you guys? Do you have any works that remind you of Lunars or inspire you with regards to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2134-fallssideways","user":"FallsSideways","date":". 02-23-2019, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2134-fallssideways","name":"FallsSideways","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:11:34-08:00","id":1291170,"title":"","content":"....I almost want to get that game just because it sounds like they got the same music group as Umineko.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, Umineko is possibly a Lunar inspiration, but telling people why is a spoiler. It's more obviously a Fair Folk thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T15:43:10-08:00","id":1291273,"title":"","content":"Given that I own a Switch and am a massive Lunar nerd, I'm obligated to research into this topic further to see if I should buy this game.<br /> <br /> I certainly ain't buying Anthem. (dammit, EA)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:11:39-08:00","id":1291279,"title":"","content":"Mestra, an obscure character from Greek mythology. From the Metamorphoses, Book 8, Lines 739-823. Mestra's Father Erysichthon is such a bastard that he was cursed with insatiable and agonizing hunger that only increased the more he ate. He had to buy so much food that sold first his kingdom and then his daughter as a slave. The gods took pity, and blessed his daughter with the ability to change into any animal or human shape so she could escape. However, being a disturbingly extreme example of Roman filial piety, she sold herself repeatedly into slavery again and again to provide her father more and more food. Eventually, his hunger is too much, and he dies attempting to devour himself.<br /> <br /> There's a Lunar mentioned in Masters of Jade named Alcina who sounds similar, btw.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:43:40-08:00","id":1291292,"title":"","content":"On a cheesier note, anyone who loves silliness and doesn't have to the time to actually read &quot;Journey to the West&quot; may want to check out the 70s Japanese tv show &quot;Monkey&quot;, a surprise hit in NZ and Australia, and its recent NZ remake, &quot;The New Legends of Monkey&quot;. The whole thing feels like extremely goofy if low powered exalted, and it's a good introduction to Sun Wukong, the archetypal Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}